    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.7, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"open_connection\", \"components\": [\"U4\", \"U8\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.2\", \"U8.2\", \"U8.4\"], \"nets\": [\"Net-(U8-Pad2)\", \"I2C_SCL\"], \"observed\": \"U4 pin 2 (SCL_{2}, the non-isolated primary-side clock pin of the EC ADM3260) is not on I2C_SCL. It sits alone on Net-(U8-Pad2) with the input of a 74LVC1G34 buffer U8. U8's output (pin 4) drives I2C_SCL, the shared main clock that also reaches U3 pin 2, M1 IO5, M4 and the pull-up R4. The EC isolator therefore never receives the bus clock, and a buffer output is driving the main bus from the EC isolator's own clock input.\", \"expected\": \"Like U3 pin 2 for the pH channel, U4 pin 2 (SCL_{2}) should sit directly on the main I2C_SCL net, so the EC isolator's primary side shares the master clock. The spec describes U3 and U4 as each bridging the non-isolated I2C bus to their isolated domain, and does not mention any buffer on the clock line.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"119\\\") (name \\\"Net-(U8-Pad2)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"U4\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"SCL_{2}\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U8\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"77\\\") (name \\\"I2C_SCL\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"H1\\\") (pin \\\"3\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U3\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"SCL_{2}\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U8\\\") (pin \\\"4\\\") (pintype \\\"output\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Primary (non-isolated) side of U3 and U4 (ADM3260 isolators), which bridge through to the isolated pH/EC domains.\"}], \"impact\": \"The EC (EZO-EC, M3) channel gets no SCL clock from the master, so EC readings fail. The buffer output also drives the shared I2C_SCL line from a path that does not carry the bus clock. This can contend with the ESP32 and U3 on the same line, and it adds an unexplained gate in the isolation path.\", \"confidence\": 0.7}], \"summary\": \"U4's primary-side SCL pin (pin 2) is not connected to the main I2C_SCL net like U3's is. It is routed through an unexplained 74LVC1G34 buffer (U8) whose output drives I2C_SCL instead, so the EC isolator is left without a clock and the buffer contends on the shared bus.\"}",
